{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויאר", :translit "va'ye'er", :gloss "and it illuminated"} {:he "ב' במסו'", :translit "b' b'meso'", :gloss "twice in the Masorah"} {:he "ויאר את הלילה", :translit "va'ye'er et ha-laylah", :gloss "and it illuminated the night"} {:he "אל ה' ויאר לנו", :translit "el ha-shem va'ye'er lanu", :gloss "to the Lord and He illuminated for us"} {:he "ויהי הענן והחושך למצרים", :translit "va'yehi ha-anan ve-ha-choshech le-mitzrayim", :gloss "and the cloud and the darkness were for the Egyptians"} {:he "שלא סר עמוד הענן כמו בשאר הלילות", :translit "she'lo sar amud ha-anan k'mo b'sha'ar ha-leilot", :gloss "that the pillar of cloud did not depart as on other nights"} {:he "אלא היה הולך לאחוריהם", :translit "elah hayah holech le'achoreihem", :gloss "but it went behind them"} {:he "כדי להחשיך למצרים", :translit "k'dei le'hachshich le-mitzrayim", :gloss "in order to darken for the Egyptians"} {:he "אבל לישראל היה אור", :translit "aval le-yisrael hayah or", :gloss "but for Israel there was light"} {:he "דכתיב אל ה' ויאר לנו", :translit "d'khatuv el ha-shem va'ye'er lanu", :gloss "as written: to the Lord and He illuminated for us"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ויאר את הלילה" "אל ה' ויאר לנו"]}], :frame {:text "The pillar of cloud that had guided Israel now repositioned between Israel and the Egyptians: it darkened the Egyptian side while illuminating the Israelite side. This double function of the cloud at the sea fulfills the phrase in Psalms 118:27, 'אל ה׳ ויאר לנו,' understood as 'to the Lord—and He illuminated for us.'", :sources ["Exodus 14:20" "Psalms 118:27"]}} {:quotes [{:he "זה אל זה", :translit "zeh el zeh", :gloss "this to that"} {:he "ב' דסמיכי דין", :translit "b' d'samikhei din", :gloss "two that are juxtaposed"} {:he "ואידך וקרא זא\"ז", :translit "ve'idach ve-kara za'az", :gloss "and the other: and one called to the other"} {:he "ק' ק' ק'", :translit "k' k' k'", :gloss "kuf kuf kuf (three verses each containing זה אל זה or זא אל זה)"} {:he "שבקשו המלאכים לומר שירה", :translit "she'bikshu ha-mal'achim leymar shirah", :gloss "that the angels sought to say song"} {:he "וא\"ל הקב\"ה", :translit "ve'amar lahem ha-kadosh baruch hu", :gloss "and the Holy One Blessed be He said to them"} {:he "מעשי ידי טובעים בים", :translit "ma'asei yadai tove'im ba-yam", :gloss "the work of My hands are drowning in the sea"} {:he "ואתם אומרים שירה", :translit "ve-atem om'rim shirah", :gloss "and you say song"} {:he "ולא קרב זה אל זה", :translit "ve-lo karav zeh el zeh", :gloss "and this did not come near that"} {:he "אותם שנאמר בהם וקרא זא אל זה", :translit "otam she'ne'emar bahem ve-kara ze el ze", :gloss "those about whom it is said: and one called to the other"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Three juxtaposed occurrences of זה אל זה / זא אל זה linked by the common phrase קרא"} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ולא קרב זה אל זה" "וקרא זא אל זה"]}], :frame {:text "When the Egyptians were drowning in the sea, the ministering angels sought to recite song before the Holy One, Blessed be He. He said to them: My handiwork is drowning in the sea, and you recite song? This is expounded from Isaiah 6:3, 'וקרא זה אל זה' — the angels calling to one another — which is linked to Exodus 14:20, 'ולא קרב זה אל זה,' Israel not approaching Egypt, because both share the phrase 'זה אל זה / זא אל זה.'", :sources ["Megillah 10b" "Sanhedrin 39b" "Isaiah 6:3" "Exodus 14:20"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ויאר את הלילה" "אל ה' ויאר לנו"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ויאר את הלילה", :refs ["Exodus 14:20"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "אל ה' ויאר לנו", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :other, :note "Three juxtaposed occurrences of זה אל זה / זא אל זה linked by the common phrase קרא", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ולא קרב זה אל זה" "וקרא זא אל זה"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ולא קרב זה אל זה", 